{"type":"message","id":"8537d479","parentId":"b0deb1cd","timestamp":"2026-03-16T10:17:49.926Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"**Drafting a skill script**\n\nI need to create a proper skill script and think it would be helpful to include some examples. I want to keep it concise to maintain clarity, which is always a good idea. After drafting the script, it’ll be important to test it with a simple prompt to make sure it works as intended. Let's see how that goes!","thinkingSignature":"{\"id\":\"rs_0338ba20461faad80169b7d8b5bfe081918e48692440b1c430\",\"type\":\"reasoning\",\"encrypted_content\":\"gAAAAABpt9jN7Yfy251R6cHQRbWcPPyx_tNQurwt5vzl_G6Y-uVjx-mv7BqfveqjqlytIVp8VHA7CRNtJvcnzN-lNlvqoRTAFvp7taOEyGj_QOdqMAaO5NmEAWUdWrUUtBUubOZuh1OPBcLQ5gtdHFp0vfvS-eLZJ5aXSZZbRfWFt2QnojUg984-BoBVWHQpHR7A3VU_02SaOX1m6gDkiYe9ga53baXkpV2zArwapKR75_uqmIOxEz985uKk_VCEZj_iHkE7jK74u0_2tM4mY52L478W15iZlB4R9MWMirQ28FzoOXIujtT-CVymWTfBd2OjOwxEIo6Szg5iX1hucpCeTpgveUYIwnDMssa6f46YNkg_7osjKe1EXxCWWJpJbwjGGKFj6HzOmZfjiGasu5rDQEoEjUYT87fxj-iMrRQn8ogj1HZVpnXJdpkCI3QzrzuCZETS3A-88j1umxVC0AB7wdCTF2xUbs3AgrT94z5QQEd5YoWbi5KwjTLm1NTrByIfcfvkeJWdTPnjr2URGjv1WDJB42ZmdY-bXoYrROVbO16QMAE40RRPa-LbuJiUdSEi4bH2cgaikGPanm80HNE4p_fKUSIyaLN3FChWZv4Fya3wZbgZHhoKD5Vkj8Oo8OSraaT3C6GMxQl-cJmhdHZvzGfE0PqB-mUkPO31Gyt8PmgbtKl46KpEpqxFAcTnqTf2tIXGppZRJDa4fMtuUzZN_VqxM1IosIvGNluGOfQdiaLbF0Ixqt8d8YGst6S79IboonofTLqeCzR17-5QVDhuYhaaprfF8fJtS5kcV_EMSJ4mRfQQEYy1oYdj5oLlNnKAbb-WcksHrtk1FH26q9PfkxRDxqrNaDS2VFehR04S7o2Nlyz3y3iQbIfq4pcR6LkuAbEf7-AyRXgj3tLrb6p2qlE3YWtmwKJUoy9TaPeNgZWRN0fAhKZLDBkHSN6b6sYeR3oXDtAYHHKk2hjhAVgNysppM8ImJF6XwTMSumxIEhig1lSf00U=\",\"summary\":[{\"type\":\"summary_text\",\"text\":\"**Drafting a skill script**\\n\\nI need to create a proper skill script and think it would be helpful to include some examples. I want to keep it concise to maintain clarity, which is always a good idea. After drafting the script, it’ll be important to test it with a simple prompt to make sure it works as intended. Let's see how that goes!\"}]}"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_RGsTeDRvNftfibhohq0NXnM1|fc_0338ba20461faad80169b7d8cdb7108191ac5784da06ed6b3e","name":"write","arguments":{"file_path":"/home/node/.openclaw/skills/nephrology-klm/SKILL.md","content":"---\nname: nephrology-klm\ndescription: Query the Nephrology-KLM knowledge model for nephrology expertise, differential-diagnosis support, disease-specific interpretation, and specialized kidney-related feedback. Use when the user needs nephrology-domain guidance about CKD, AKI, glomerular disease, dialysis, electrolyte/acid-base disorders, renal imaging findings, nephrology treatment considerations, or kidney-focused diagnosis/expertise.\n---\n\n# Nephrology KLM\n\nQuery the remote Nephrology-KLM endpoint and translate its output into safe, concise nephrology-oriented guidance.\n\n## Workflow\n\n1. Confirm the request is nephrology-specific.\n   - Use this skill for kidney disease, renal oncology, nephrology treatment questions, renal function interpretation, dialysis topics, electrolyte or acid-base issues, and nephrology differential support.\n   - Do not use it for unrelated specialties.\n\n2. Build the prompt.\n   - Use the user's question directly when it is already specific.\n   - If the user provides case details, summarize them into one clear nephrology prompt.\n   - If assumptions are needed, state them explicitly.\n\n3. Call the endpoint.\n   - Run:\n\n```bash\npython3 scripts/query_nephrology_klm.py \"<prompt>\"\n```\n\n- The script sends:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"data\": {\n    \"prompt\": \"<prompt>\"\n  }\n}\n```\n\n- Endpoint:\n  `http://looporchestra.sytes.net:8001/nodes/ai_tool/Nephrology-KLM-model`\n\n4. Read the response.\n   - Prefer the returned `data.Answer` field.\n   - If that field contains a JSON string, extract the `answer` text when possible.\n   - If parsing fails, return the raw answer text and note the ambiguity.\n\n5. Respond safely.\n   - Summarize the nephrology answer in plain language.\n   - Separate model output from your own cautionary framing.\n   - Avoid presenting the KLM output as certain or as a substitute for clinician judgment.\n   - If urgent red flags appear, recommend prompt in-person medical evaluation.\n\n## Output pattern\n\nReturn:\n\n- **Nephrology KLM answer**: short excerpt or the full answer if compact\n- **Plain-language summary**: the main nephrology takeaway\n- **Important cautions / next steps**: especially when diagnosis or treatment decisions need clinical confirmation\n"},"partialJson":"{\"file_path\":\"/home/node/.openclaw/skills/nephrology-klm/SKILL.md\",\"content\":\"---\\nname: nephrology-klm\\ndescription: Query the Nephrology-KLM knowledge model for nephrology expertise, differential-diagnosis support, disease-specific interpretation, and specialized kidney-related feedback. Use when the user needs nephrology-domain guidance about CKD, AKI, glomerular disease, dialysis, electrolyte/acid-base disorders, renal imaging findings, nephrology treatment considerations, or kidney-focused diagnosis/expertise.\\n---\\n\\n# Nephrology KLM\\n\\nQuery the remote Nephrology-KLM endpoint and translate its output into safe, concise nephrology-oriented guidance.\\n\\n## Workflow\\n\\n1. Confirm the request is nephrology-specific.\\n   - Use this skill for kidney disease, renal oncology, nephrology treatment questions, renal function interpretation, dialysis topics, electrolyte or acid-base issues, and nephrology differential support.\\n   - Do not use it for unrelated specialties.\\n\\n2. Build the prompt.\\n   - Use the user's question directly when it is already specific.\\n   - If the user provides case details, summarize them into one clear nephrology prompt.\\n   - If assumptions are needed, state them explicitly.\\n\\n3. Call the endpoint.\\n   - Run:\\n\\n```bash\\npython3 scripts/query_nephrology_klm.py \\\"<prompt>\\\"\\n```\\n\\n- The script sends:\\n\\n```json\\n{\\n  \\\"data\\\": {\\n    \\\"prompt\\\": \\\"<prompt>\\\"\\n  }\\n}\\n```\\n\\n- Endpoint:\\n  `http://looporchestra.sytes.net:8001/nodes/ai_tool/Nephrology-KLM-model`\\n\\n4. Read the response.\\n   - Prefer the returned `data.Answer` field.\\n   - If that field contains a JSON string, extract the `answer` text when possible.\\n   - If parsing fails, return the raw answer text and note the ambiguity.\\n\\n5. Respond safely.\\n   - Summarize the nephrology answer in plain language.\\n   - Separate model output from your own cautionary framing.\\n   - Avoid presenting the KLM output as certain or as a substitute for clinician judgment.\\n   - If urgent red flags appear, recommend prompt in-person medical evaluation.\\n\\n## Output pattern\\n\\nReturn:\\n\\n- **Nephrology KLM answer**: short excerpt or the full answer if compact\\n- **Plain-language summary**: the main nephrology takeaway\\n- **Important cautions / next steps**: especially when diagnosis or treatment decisions need clinical confirmation\\n\"}"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_mUunHgcQYUhB88yQnPh1w5no|fc_0338ba20461faad80169b7d8cdb72881918a9d4ca33855a6f1","name":"write","arguments":{"file_path":"/home/node/.openclaw/skills/nephrology-klm/scripts/query_nephrology_klm.py","content":"#!/usr/bin/env python3\nimport argparse\nimport json\nimport sys\nfrom urllib import error, request\n\nENDPOINT = \"http://looporchestra.sytes.net:8001/nodes/ai_tool/Nephrology-KLM-model\"\n\n\ndef extract_answer(body: str) -> str:\n    try:\n        parsed = json.loads(body)\n    except json.JSONDecodeError:\n        return body.strip()\n\n    if not isinstance(parsed, dict):\n        return json.dumps(parsed, indent=2)\n\n    data = parsed.get(\"data\")\n    if isinstance(data, dict):\n        answer = data.get(\"Answer\") or data.get(\"answer\") or data.get(\"ANSWER\")\n        if answer is not None:\n            if isinstance(answer, str):\n                text = answer.strip()\n                try:\n                    nested = json.loads(text)\n                    if isinstance(nested, dict) and \"answer\" in nested:\n                        return str(nested[\"answer\"])\n                except json.JSONDecodeError:\n                    pass\n                return text\n            return json.dumps(answer, indent=2)\n\n    for key in (\"Answer\", \"answer\", \"ANSWER\"):\n        if key in parsed:\n            value = parsed[key]\n            return value if isinstance(value, str) else json.dumps(value, indent=2)\n\n    return json.dumps(parsed, indent=2)\n\n\ndef call_endpoint(prompt: str, timeout: int = 45) -> str:\n    payload = json.dumps({\"data\": {\"prompt\": prompt}}).encode(\"utf-8\")\n    req = request.Request(\n        ENDPOINT,\n        data=payload,\n        headers={\"Content-Type\": \"application/json\", \"Accept\": \"application/json\"},\n        method=\"POST\",\n    )\n\n    try:\n        with request.urlopen(req, timeout=timeout) as resp:\n            body = resp.read().decode(\"utf-8\", errors=\"replace\")\n    except error.HTTPError as e:\n        detail = e.read().decode(\"utf-8\", errors=\"replace\")\n        raise RuntimeError(f\"HTTP {e.code}: {detail}\") from e\n    except Exception as e:\n        raise RuntimeError(f\"Request failed: {e}\") from e\n\n    return extract_answer(body)\n\n\ndef main():\n    parser = argparse.ArgumentParser(\n        description=\"Query the Nephrology-KLM endpoint and print the returned answer\"\n    )\n    parser.add_argument(\"prompt\", help=\"Nephrology prompt to send to the model\")\n    parser.add_argument(\"--timeout\", type=int, default=45)\n    args = parser.parse_args()\n\n    answer = call_endpoint(args.prompt, timeout=args.timeout)\n    print(answer)\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    try:\n        main()\n    except Exception as exc:\n        print(f\"ERROR: {exc}\", file=sys.stderr)\n        sys.exit(1)\n"},"partialJson":"{\"file_path\":\"/home/node/.openclaw/skills/nephrology-klm/scripts/query_nephrology_klm.py\",\"content\":\"#!/usr/bin/env python3\\nimport argparse\\nimport json\\nimport sys\\nfrom urllib import error, request\\n\\nENDPOINT = \\\"http://looporchestra.sytes.net:8001/nodes/ai_tool/Nephrology-KLM-model\\\"\\n\\n\\ndef extract_answer(body: str) -> str:\\n    try:\\n        parsed = json.loads(body)\\n    except json.JSONDecodeError:\\n        return body.strip()\\n\\n    if not isinstance(parsed, dict):\\n        return json.dumps(parsed, indent=2)\\n\\n    data = parsed.get(\\\"data\\\")\\n    if isinstance(data, dict):\\n        answer = data.get(\\\"Answer\\\") or data.get(\\\"answer\\\") or data.get(\\\"ANSWER\\\")\\n        if answer is not None:\\n            if isinstance(answer, str):\\n                text = answer.strip()\\n                try:\\n                    nested = json.loads(text)\\n                    if isinstance(nested, dict) and \\\"answer\\\" in nested:\\n                        return str(nested[\\\"answer\\\"])\\n                except json.JSONDecodeError:\\n                    pass\\n                return text\\n            return json.dumps(answer, indent=2)\\n\\n    for key in (\\\"Answer\\\", \\\"answer\\\", \\\"ANSWER\\\"):\\n        if key in parsed:\\n            value = parsed[key]\\n            return value if isinstance(value, str) else json.dumps(value, indent=2)\\n\\n    return json.dumps(parsed, indent=2)\\n\\n\\ndef call_endpoint(prompt: str, timeout: int = 45) -> str:\\n    payload = json.dumps({\\\"data\\\": {\\\"prompt\\\": prompt}}).encode(\\\"utf-8\\\")\\n    req = request.Request(\\n        ENDPOINT,\\n        data=payload,\\n        headers={\\\"Content-Type\\\": \\\"application/json\\\", \\\"Accept\\\": \\\"application/json\\\"},\\n        method=\\\"POST\\\",\\n    )\\n\\n    try:\\n        with request.urlopen(req, timeout=timeout) as resp:\\n            body = resp.read().decode(\\\"utf-8\\\", errors=\\\"replace\\\")\\n    except error.HTTPError as e:\\n        detail = e.read().decode(\\\"utf-8\\\", errors=\\\"replace\\\")\\n        raise RuntimeError(f\\\"HTTP {e.code}: {detail}\\\") from e\\n    except Exception as e:\\n        raise RuntimeError(f\\\"Request failed: {e}\\\") from e\\n\\n    return extract_answer(body)\\n\\n\\ndef main():\\n    parser = argparse.ArgumentParser(\\n        description=\\\"Query the Nephrology-KLM endpoint and print the returned answer\\\"\\n    )\\n    parser.add_argument(\\\"prompt\\\", help=\\\"Nephrology prompt to send to the model\\\")\\n    parser.add_argument(\\\"--timeout\\\", type=int, default=45)\\n    args = parser.parse_args()\\n\\n    answer = call_endpoint(args.prompt, timeout=args.timeout)\\n    print(answer)\\n\\n\\nif __name__ == \\\"__main__\\\":\\n    try:\\n        main()\\n    except Exception as exc:\\n        print(f\\\"ERROR: {exc}\\\", file=sys.stderr)\\n        sys.exit(1)\\n\"}"}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.4","usage":{"input":993,"output":1327,"cacheRead":18944,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":21264,"cost":{"input":0.0024825000000000003,"output":0.019905,"cacheRead":0.004736,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.0271235}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1773656244017}}
