{"type":"message","id":"ceeef9ad","parentId":"ea648598","timestamp":"2026-03-16T10:18:38.463Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_2jSN1EJ2IVnAYAxonVJO8WOo|fc_0338ba20461faad80169b7d8fc3224819180851cd739752cdf","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"python3 /home/node/.openclaw/skills/nephrology-klm/scripts/query_nephrology_klm.py \"What treatment options are there for CKD with proteinuria?\" | sed -n '1,80p' && echo '\n--- REPACKAGE ---' && python3 /app/skills/skill-creator/scripts/package_skill.py /home/node/.openclaw/skills/nephrology-klm","workdir":"/home/node/.openclaw/workspace","yieldMs":10000,"timeout":120},"partialJson":"{\"command\":\"python3 /home/node/.openclaw/skills/nephrology-klm/scripts/query_nephrology_klm.py \\\"What treatment options are there for CKD with proteinuria?\\\" | sed -n '1,80p' && echo '\\n--- REPACKAGE ---' && python3 /app/skills/skill-creator/scripts/package_skill.py /home/node/.openclaw/skills/nephrology-klm\",\"workdir\":\"/home/node/.openclaw/workspace\",\"yieldMs\":10000,\"timeout\":120}"}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.4","usage":{"input":159,"output":126,"cacheRead":23552,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":23837,"cost":{"input":0.0003975,"output":0.00189,"cacheRead":0.005888,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.0081755}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1773656313324}}
{"type":"message","id":"0fdc1d0b","parentId":"ceeef9ad","timestamp":"2026-03-16T10:18:38.841Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_2jSN1EJ2IVnAYAxonVJO8WOo|fc_0338ba20461faad80169b7d8fc3224819180851cd739752cdf","toolName":"exec","content":[{"type":"text","text":"CLINICAL ANSWER\nTreatment options by active condition:\n  Chronic Kidney Disease:\n    • SGLT2 Inhibitors — Dapagliflozin (DAPA-CKD) and canagliflozin (CREDENCE) show significant renoprotection in CKD with proteinuria regardless of diabetes status\n    • Finerenone (Non-steroidal MRA) — Finerenone added to ACEi/ARB reduces CKD progression and cardiovascular events in diabetic CKD (T2DM with proteinuria)\n    • ACE Inhibitors — First-line renoprotective therapy for proteinuric CKD; reduces intraglomerular hypertension\n  If disease progresses:\n    • End-Stage Renal Disease: Kidney Transplantation\n    • Metastatic RCC: Pembrolizumab plus Lenvatinib\n    • Metastatic RCC: Ipilimumab plus Nivolumab\n\nEVIDENCE SUMMARY\n  • SGLT2 Inhibitors: Dapagliflozin (DAPA-CKD) and canagliflozin (CREDENCE) show significant renoprotection in CKD with proteinuria regardless of diabetes status\n  • Finerenone (Non-steroidal MRA): Finerenone added to ACEi/ARB reduces CKD progression and cardiovascular events in diabetic CKD (T2DM with proteinuria)\n  • Kidney Transplantation: Preferred treatment for eligible patients; superior survival compared to dialysis\n\nPATIENT-SPECIFIC NOTE\n  • Tumor stage T1b — consider nephron-sparing options\n  • Renal function: eGFR:58 mL/min/1.73m² — relevant to systemic therapy dosing\n  • BP 138/84 — hypertension management relevant to treatment selection\n  • Pathogenic VHL variant — belzutifan FDA-approved for VHL-associated RCC\n  • PBRM1 VUS — may influence immunotherapy response; discuss with MDT\n\nRED FLAGS\n  • No knowledge conflicts detected across KLMs\n\nRECOMMENDED NEXT STEPS\n  • Confirm treatment eligibility with multidisciplinary oncology team\n  • Partial nephrectomy preferred for T1 lesions (nephron-sparing)\n  • Evaluate belzutifan eligibility (FDA-approved for VHL-associated RCC)\n  • Monitor renal function (eGFR:58 mL/min/1.73m²) — CKD staging affects systemic therapy choice\n\n--- REPACKAGE ---\nPackaging skill: /home/node/.openclaw/skills/nephrology-klm\n\nValidating skill...\n[OK] Skill is valid!\n\n  Added: nephrology-klm/SKILL.md\n  Added: nephrology-klm/scripts/query_nephrology_klm.py\n\n[OK] Successfully packaged skill to: /home/node/.openclaw/workspace/nephrology-klm.skill"}],"details":{"status":"completed","exitCode":0,"durationMs":373,"aggregated":"CLINICAL ANSWER\nTreatment options by active condition:\n  Chronic Kidney Disease:\n    • SGLT2 Inhibitors — Dapagliflozin (DAPA-CKD) and canagliflozin (CREDENCE) show significant renoprotection in CKD with proteinuria regardless of diabetes status\n    • Finerenone (Non-steroidal MRA) — Finerenone added to ACEi/ARB reduces CKD progression and cardiovascular events in diabetic CKD (T2DM with proteinuria)\n    • ACE Inhibitors — First-line renoprotective therapy for proteinuric CKD; reduces intraglomerular hypertension\n  If disease progresses:\n    • End-Stage Renal Disease: Kidney Transplantation\n    • Metastatic RCC: Pembrolizumab plus Lenvatinib\n    • Metastatic RCC: Ipilimumab plus Nivolumab\n\nEVIDENCE SUMMARY\n  • SGLT2 Inhibitors: Dapagliflozin (DAPA-CKD) and canagliflozin (CREDENCE) show significant renoprotection in CKD with proteinuria regardless of diabetes status\n  • Finerenone (Non-steroidal MRA): Finerenone added to ACEi/ARB reduces CKD progression and cardiovascular events in diabetic CKD (T2DM with proteinuria)\n  • Kidney Transplantation: Preferred treatment for eligible patients; superior survival compared to dialysis\n\nPATIENT-SPECIFIC NOTE\n  • Tumor stage T1b — consider nephron-sparing options\n  • Renal function: eGFR:58 mL/min/1.73m² — relevant to systemic therapy dosing\n  • BP 138/84 — hypertension management relevant to treatment selection\n  • Pathogenic VHL variant — belzutifan FDA-approved for VHL-associated RCC\n  • PBRM1 VUS — may influence immunotherapy response; discuss with MDT\n\nRED FLAGS\n  • No knowledge conflicts detected across KLMs\n\nRECOMMENDED NEXT STEPS\n  • Confirm treatment eligibility with multidisciplinary oncology team\n  • Partial nephrectomy preferred for T1 lesions (nephron-sparing)\n  • Evaluate belzutifan eligibility (FDA-approved for VHL-associated RCC)\n  • Monitor renal function (eGFR:58 mL/min/1.73m²) — CKD staging affects systemic therapy choice\n\n--- REPACKAGE ---\nPackaging skill: /home/node/.openclaw/skills/nephrology-klm\n\nValidating skill...\n[OK] Skill is valid!\n\n  Added: nephrology-klm/SKILL.md\n  Added: nephrology-klm/scripts/query_nephrology_klm.py\n\n[OK] Successfully packaged skill to: /home/node/.openclaw/workspace/nephrology-klm.skill","cwd":"/home/node/.openclaw/workspace"},"isError":false,"timestamp":1773656318838}}
